  "_source": "Sali & Toraman, Navigating the Unknown: Intent Classification and Out-of-Distribution Detection Using Large Language Models, Findings EMNLP 2025, https://aclanthology.org/2025.findings-emnlp.791/. Instructions = the paper's zero-shot system prompt, Appendix A.3 (p. 14662-14663), verbatim with PDF line breaks re-joined; its last line ('Remember that you need to choose intents via tool calling only.') is replaced by one sentence naming the state field, because Jev's choice primitive replaces tool calling. Zero-shot setting (Section 3.3.2, Appendix A.2): each intent is given by its name only (tool name = intent name, empty description) plus a 'fallback' tool for OOD. Criteria keys are the released intent names verbatim (CLINC150 clinc/oos-eval@828f809 data_full.json; BANKING77 PolyAI-LDN/task-specific-datasets@57ec275 banking_data); each criterion text is only the name with underscores replaced by spaces (no descriptions exist in the paper or datasets). The fallback criterion paraphrases A.3 step 3 ('If it does not match any of the provided intents, classify it as \"fallback\"'). Per request, the choice offers only the ID intents of a frozen partition (data/frozen/nav_unknown/splits.json) plus 'fallback'.",
